/**
 * Postgres-backed implementation of the Drift repository.
 *
 * Logic mirrors `repo.sqlite.ts` 1-for-1; only the column types and the
 * upsert clause differ. Postgres returns native Date objects for
 * timestamp columns (vs. the SQLite ISO string) and emits UUIDs from a
 * server-side `uuid_generate_v4()` default rather than the application
 * generating them with `randomUUID()`.
 *
 * Kept separate from the SQLite impl so any future per-driver quirk
 * (jsonb cast, ON CONFLICT clause, RETURNING semantics) stays explicit
